coverage:
I read the whole LaTeX source (intro, preliminaries, reduction, jet-tools, geometry, frobenius, completion, positive) and checked these in detail:
(1) The ray-length bound for generalized klt (Lemma generalized-ray-bound), done by perturbing to an ordinary klt boundary.
(2) The two-program construction. The inequality (1-s0/s)/d > 4n s0/s forces U-triviality, and the full-nef-dimension transfer through the effective exceptional comparisons holds.
(3) Prop full-positive. Restriction to fibres, then generic-fibre bigness via semicontinuity, then the convex-combination step.
(4) Lemma bounded-curves. The BZ birationality step and the Khovanskii–Teissier chain P·H^{f-1} ≤ P^f (H·P^{f-1}/P^f)^{f-1} are both correct.
(5) Scalar bound. The levels 1.5ρ to 3.5ρ lie below 4ρ, and the zero-dimensional case gives (k/h0)^n P^n < 1.
(6) Bundle volume estimates. Checked the one-ξ term, the bound on powers of q/r, and the cancellation of q in the w=0 slice case.
(7) Slice-fibre case analysis:
- generically finite onto a proper image;
- P^1-bundle over W0 (expansion with pseudo-effective K and nef classes);
- multisection: D1−D2 ~ eL, κ(bG)>0 via the negativity lemma, then the terminal discrepancy comparison;
- sweeping branch divisors: Hodge index J^2P^{n-2} ≤ (JP^{n-1})^2/P^n, and the ramification divisor bounded by the effective K_{V*};
- fixed covers: Hanamura gives an abelian model, N0 is big by the Hermitian-form kernel argument, so K+uL0 is big.
(8) Frobenius theorem:
- the triangular product-jet argument;
- the coefficient-of-1 projection in A*[z]/(z^p−z0^p), which gives generic rank p^{2n};
- the diagonal rank bound ≤ h^0(Δ_F, L_p) via flat base change;
- the graded pieces A_j(Ω) and the socle pairing;
- the Langer-based slope bound μ_max(A_j) ≤ (p−1)K·C + nc;
- the lattice count giving 7^n p^{2n} H^n;
- the determinant class c1(Q_i)/R = B_p/p + (p−1)K/2p + λ_i S;
- the two order bounds, 80ε vs 3/4.
(9) Application. D+ = 2D+E, the order bound 8ρ < 16ε, BDPP for the movable class, and the pseudo-effective difference w^*(P−λL)+E/2.
(10) Completion. Index-one cover plus terminalization, and the boundary perturbation via Lemma two-nef-model, with B_Y = 0.
(11) Positive-part descent. Nef reduction, LP Lemma 3.1, Hacon–Xu relative good model, Ambro's formula, the Pic^0 descent, and the field transfer.
I found no step that fails. Where I could test the Frobenius incompatibility theorem on product abelian surfaces with non-full-dimension S, its hypotheses fail for elementary reasons, which is consistent with the theorem.
